Allow android_ndk_repository to fetch a pinned NDK itself.

Upstream resolves the NDK from ANDROID_NDK_HOME or an absolute `path`, so the
C++ half of an APK build depends on whatever each machine and CI runner has
installed. Every other toolchain here is pinned, and the NDK decides which ABIs
an APK carries -- getting it wrong ships an app that cannot install.

This cannot be solved from a module extension. A repo an extension declares
does not exist until the extension RETURNS, so its path cannot be resolved from
inside it, and module_ctx.download_and_extract refuses to write outside a
repository directory. A repository rule may write into its own directory, so
the download belongs here.

The archive unpacks into ndk_dist/ rather than the repository root, because
_create_symlinks writes "sources", "ndk/sources" and the toolchain paths into
that root -- an NDK unpacked there would be symlinking onto itself. With the
NDK one level down, the existing symlink logic is reused unchanged.

`local` becomes False: a local=True repo is refetched every build, which with a
url would mean re-extracting ~1GB each time. Path-based use is unaffected in
practice -- an NDK is a fixed directory, not a tree edited between builds.

Offered upstream rather than carried indefinitely; rebase when bumping the
module version.

--- a/rules.bzl	2026-09-22 08:14:07
+++ b/rules.bzl	2026-09-22 08:17:11
@@ -23,12 +23,26 @@
     Returns:
         A final dict of configuration attributes and values.
     """
-    ndk_path = ctx.attr.path or ctx.getenv("ANDROID_NDK_HOME", None)
-    if not ndk_path:
-        fail("Either the ANDROID_NDK_HOME environment variable or the " +
-             "path attribute of android_ndk_repository must be set.")
-    if ndk_path.startswith("$WORKSPACE_ROOT"):
-        ndk_path = str(ctx.workspace_root) + ndk_path.removeprefix("$WORKSPACE_ROOT")
+    if ctx.attr.url:
+        # Into this repository's own directory, which is the one place a
+        # repository rule is allowed to write.
+        # Into a subdirectory, not the repository root: _create_symlinks
+        # below writes "sources", "ndk/sources" and the toolchain paths into
+        # the root, and an NDK unpacked there would be symlinking onto itself.
+        ctx.download_and_extract(
+            url = ctx.attr.url,
+            output = "ndk_dist",
+            sha256 = ctx.attr.sha256,
+            stripPrefix = ctx.attr.strip_prefix,
+        )
+        ndk_path = str(ctx.path("ndk_dist")) + "/"
+    else:
+        ndk_path = ctx.attr.path or ctx.getenv("ANDROID_NDK_HOME", None)
+        if not ndk_path:
+            fail("Either the ANDROID_NDK_HOME environment variable, or the " +
+                 "path or url attribute of android_ndk_repository, must be set.")
+        if ndk_path.startswith("$WORKSPACE_ROOT"):
+            ndk_path = str(ctx.workspace_root) + ndk_path.removeprefix("$WORKSPACE_ROOT")
 
     is_windows = False
     executable_extension = ""
@@ -127,6 +141,9 @@
 android_ndk_repository = repository_rule(
     attrs = {
         "path": attr.string(),
+        "url": attr.string(doc = "Fetch the NDK from here instead of using a local one."),
+        "sha256": attr.string(doc = "Checksum of the archive at url."),
+        "strip_prefix": attr.string(doc = "Leading directory to strip from the archive."),
         "api_level": attr.int(),
         "_build": attr.label(default = ":BUILD", allow_single_file = True),
         "_template_ndk_root": attr.label(default = ":BUILD.ndk_root.tpl", allow_single_file = True),
@@ -134,6 +151,6 @@
         "_template_ndk_clang": attr.label(default = ":BUILD.ndk_clang.tpl", allow_single_file = True),
         "_template_ndk_sysroot": attr.label(default = ":BUILD.ndk_sysroot.tpl", allow_single_file = True),
     },
-    local = True,
+    local = False,
     implementation = _android_ndk_repository_impl,
 )
